menu "OpenShock OTA"

    config OPENSHOCK_OTA_GZIP
        bool "Try the gzip app image (the binary URL + .gz) first"
        default y
        help
            Decompressed with zlib (espressif/zlib), compressed with a 4 KB window. The decoder and its
            window are allocated before the downloads start; without the memory the plain image is
            downloaded instead.

    config OPENSHOCK_OTA_GZIP_MIN_FREE_BLOCK
        int "Largest free block to keep after allocating the gzip decoder (bytes)"
        range 16384 131072
        default 40960
        help
            The decoder is freed again, and the plain image downloaded, unless this much contiguous
            internal RAM is left for the TLS connections to the download host. Unused without
            OPENSHOCK_OTA_GZIP; not hidden behind it, so the decoder compiles either way.

endmenu
